    "content": "The World Baseball Classic (WBC), launched in 2006, is the premier international professional baseball tournament sanctioned by the WBSC. Featuring MLB and international league players, it was created to promote global baseball. Japan leads with three titles, followed by USA, Dominican Republic, and 2026 champions Venezuela. This video explains the context and significance of the World Baseball Classic: Key Moments and Evolution: 2006: Japan wins the inaugural tournament, defeating Cuba. 2009: Japan repeats as champions, beating South Korea. 2013: The Dominican Republic wins the title undefeated. 2017: The United States wins its first championship, defeating Puerto Rico. 2023: Japan wins a record-extending third title, featuring a dramatic showdown with the U.S. in the final. Shohei Ohtani named MVP. 2026: Venezuela defeats the United States 3-2 to win its first title, with Garcia named MVP. Tournament Growth: The tournament shifted to a mostly four-year cycle, with the 2021 event delayed to 2023 due to COVID-19. The field expanded from 16 to 20 teams for the 2023 tournament, increasing international competition. The 2026 USA-Dominican Republic semifinal set a new record for the most-watched WBC broadcast. Champions History: 2006: Japan 2009: Japan 2013: Dominican Republic 2017: United States 2023: Japan 2026: Venezuela",
